<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Paul III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1468">1468</a>–1549</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Alessandro Farnese, Alessandro Farnese (pope)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Paul III, born Alessandro Farnese, was pope from 1534 to 1549. He approved the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jesuits">Jesuits</a>, called the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/council-of-trent">Council of Trent</a> and began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/counter-reformation">Catholic Reformation</a>, but also advanced his family, creating the duchies of Castro and of Parma and Piacenza for his son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pier-luigi-farnese">Pier Luigi Farnese</a>. He brought Perugia and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/camerino">Camerino</a> under direct papal control.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-paul-iii.jpg" alt="Pope Paul III" width="320" height="418" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Titian · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Portrait_of_Pope_Paul_III_Farnese_(by_Titian)_-_National_Museum_of_Capodimonte.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
